<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<spec xmlns="https://vibevm.org/spec/1">
  <title id="org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--root">Flow: Atomic Commits</title>
  <status stage="impl" state="done"/>
  <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--THE-PROJECT-USES-THE-ATOMIC-COMMITS-DISCIPLINE fact="true" status="impl/done">This project uses the **atomic commits** discipline as its Git
contract.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--THE-PROJECT-USES-THE-ATOMIC-COMMITS-DISCIPLINE></p>
  <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--ONE-COMMIT-ONE-IDEA-AND-THE-MESSAGE-EXPLAINS-WHY fact="true" status="impl/done">One commit carries exactly one idea, and the commit message
explains *why*.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--ONE-COMMIT-ONE-IDEA-AND-THE-MESSAGE-EXPLAINS-WHY></p>
  <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--core-rule title="Core rule">
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--ONE-COMMIT-EQUALS-ONE-LOGICAL-CHANGE fact="true" status="impl/done">**One commit = one logical change**, not one file changed.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--ONE-COMMIT-EQUALS-ONE-LOGICAL-CHANGE></p>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--A-MIXED-SESSION-IS-THREE-COMMITS fact="true" status="impl/done">A session that produces (a) a typo fix, (b) a refactor, and (c) a
schema update is **three** commits, not one.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--A-MIXED-SESSION-IS-THREE-COMMITS></p>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--A-COHERENT-FIFTEEN-FILE-CHANGE-IS-ONE-COMMIT fact="true" status="impl/done">A feature that touches
fifteen files for one coherent reason is **one** commit, not fifteen.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--A-COHERENT-FIFTEEN-FILE-CHANGE-IS-ONE-COMMIT></p>
  </org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--core-rule>
  <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--message-format title="Message format">
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--COMMIT-MESSAGES-FOLLOW-THE-CONVENTIONAL-COMMITS-FLOW fact="true" status="impl/done">Commit messages follow the **git-conventional-commits** flow — a sibling package:
`spec://org.vibevm.world/git-conventional-commits/flows/conventional-commits/conventional-commits#root`.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--COMMIT-MESSAGES-FOLLOW-THE-CONVENTIONAL-COMMITS-FLOW></p>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--CONVENTIONAL-COMMITS-IS-THE-FORMAT-THIS-FLOW-IS-THE-ATOMICITY fact="true" status="impl/done">Conventional Commits is the *format*; this flow is the *atomicity* (one commit, one idea).</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--CONVENTIONAL-COMMITS-IS-THE-FORMAT-THIS-FLOW-IS-THE-ATOMICITY></p>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--THE-TWO-ARE-DISTINCT-AND-RUN-TOGETHER fact="true" status="impl/done">The
two are distinct and run together — a `feat: add foo, bar, baz` message is valid Conventional
Commits and a violation of the atomic rule.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--THE-TWO-ARE-DISTINCT-AND-RUN-TOGETHER></p>
  </org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--message-format>
  <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--session-end title="Session end">
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--before-closing-a-session-lead fact="true" status="impl/done">Before closing a session:</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--before-closing-a-session-lead></p>
    <facts ordered="true">
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-RUN-STATUS-AND-DIFF-AND-NAME-EVERY-CHANGE fact="true" status="impl/done">Run `git status` and `git diff HEAD`. Name every change by intent.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-RUN-STATUS-AND-DIFF-AND-NAME-EVERY-CHANGE>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-GROUP-CHANGES-INTO-ATOMIC-COMMITS fact="true" status="impl/done">Group changes into atomic commits — one commit per intent, not per
   file.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-GROUP-CHANGES-INTO-ATOMIC-COMMITS>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-STAGE-AND-COMMIT-EACH-GROUP-SEPARATELY fact="true" status="impl/done">Stage and commit each group separately with a well-formed message.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-STAGE-AND-COMMIT-EACH-GROUP-SEPARATELY>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-DO-NOT-AMEND-OR-FORCE-PUSH-PUSHED-COMMITS fact="true" status="impl/done">Do not amend or force-push commits that are already pushed; create a
   new commit instead, unless the human explicitly approves history
   rewriting.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--STEP-DO-NOT-AMEND-OR-FORCE-PUSH-PUSHED-COMMITS>
    </facts>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--splitting-procedure-pointer fact="true" status="impl/done">Procedure for splitting a messy working tree:
@spec://org.vibevm.world/git-atomic-commits/flows/atomic-commits/splitting-large-changes#root.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--splitting-procedure-pointer></p>
  </org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--session-end>
  <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--why-human-ai-teams title="Why this matters in a human-AI team">
    <facts ordered="false">
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-DIFF-AS-VERIFICATION fact="true" status="spec/done">**Diff as verification.** Humans verify code by reading diffs. A
  diff that mixes three concerns is not verifiable in one pass.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-DIFF-AS-VERIFICATION>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-ROLLBACK-PRECISION fact="true" status="impl/done">**Rollback precision.** `git revert &lt;sha&gt;` must undo the wrong
  thing without also undoing two correct things.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-ROLLBACK-PRECISION>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-COMMIT-LOG-AS-DECISION-RECORD fact="true" status="impl/done">**Commit log as decision record.** The message is the only place
  where *why* survives after volatile session notes and spec prose decay.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--WHY-COMMIT-LOG-AS-DECISION-RECORD>
    </facts>
    <p><org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--full-protocol-pointer fact="true" status="impl/done">Full rationale: @spec://org.vibevm.world/git-atomic-commits/flows/atomic-commits/ATOMIC-COMMITS-PROTOCOL#root.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--full-protocol-pointer></p>
  </org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--why-human-ai-teams>
  <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--never title="Never">
    <facts ordered="false">
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-MIX-REFACTOR-FEATURE-DOCS-AND-BUGFIX fact="true" status="impl/done">Never mix refactor + feature + docs + bugfix in one commit.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-MIX-REFACTOR-FEATURE-DOCS-AND-BUGFIX>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-WRITE-A-SUBJECT-THAT-SUMMARISES-WHAT-CHANGED fact="true" status="impl/done">Never write a subject that summarises *what* changed — the diff does
  that. Write *why*.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-WRITE-A-SUBJECT-THAT-SUMMARISES-WHAT-CHANGED>
      <org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-AMEND-A-PUSHED-COMMIT-WITHOUT-HUMAN-APPROVAL fact="true" status="impl/done">Never `git commit --amend` on a pushed commit without explicit human
  approval. Same for `git push --force`.</org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--NEVER-AMEND-A-PUSHED-COMMIT-WITHOUT-HUMAN-APPROVAL>
    </facts>
  </org-vibevm-world--git-atomic-commits--never>
</spec>

